HST Office: a ribbon toolbox does not reload its command images from a view frame that is closing.

The ribbon's collapse ladder (vcl HstRibbonLadder.cxx) sends DataChanged(NONE) to a toolbox whose
button size it changes, and SidebarToolBox::ChangedDataHandler then reloads the command images
(ChangedIconHandler) for the frame of SfxViewFrame::Current(). SfxBaseController::dispose clears that
SfxFrame's frame interface before SfxFrame::DoClose_Impl, so while a view frame closes its frame
interface is empty, and vcl::CommandInfoProvider::GetXGraphicForCommand calls getController()
through it.

That happens when a document is closed from another thread (UNO bridge, automation): the request
thread disposes the sidebar in DoClose_Impl, a window destroyed there is handed to the main thread
with SendMessage, which releases the SolarMutex, and the main thread handles a pending resize; the
ladder steps and the toolbox reads the empty frame. Windows r1-auto W4 (Writer, then Sheets, closed
over UNO) died this way at every run (ProcDump full dumps, runs 42779319665 and 42781778730: main
thread WM_SIZE -> layout -> ToolBox::DataChanged -> SidebarToolBox handlers -> GetImageForCommand ->
GetXGraphicForCommand, read of address 0; request thread in SfxBaseModel::close -> DoClose_Impl ->
~SidebarChildWindow -> vcl::Window::dispose waiting for the SolarMutex). The office's own crash
handler then faulted as well, so the office exited with 255 and left no dump.

ChangedIconHandler now keeps the current images when the frame interface is empty: the view is
going away.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/sfx2/source/sidebar/SidebarToolBox.cxx
+++ b/sfx2/source/sidebar/SidebarToolBox.cxx
@@ -276,16 +276,21 @@
             // The button should show the last function that was selected from the
             // dropdown. The controller should know better than us what it was.
             xController->updateImage();
         }
         else if (SfxViewFrame* pViewFrm = SfxViewFrame::Current())
         {
             OUString aCommandURL = GetItemCommand(it.first);
             css::uno::Reference<frame::XFrame> xFrame = pViewFrm->GetFrame().GetFrameInterface();
+            // HST Office: a view frame that is being closed has no frame interface any more
+            // (SfxBaseController::dispose clears it before SfxFrame::DoClose_Impl), and the command
+            // image lookup dereferences the frame: keep the current images
+            if (!xFrame.is())
+                continue;
             Image aImage = vcl::CommandInfoProvider::GetImageForCommand(aCommandURL, xFrame, GetImageSize());
             // HST Office: commands of extensions have no command image; the image the .ui file names
             // is loaded again from the new icon theme (e.g. HST after HST (dark)).
             if (!aImage && !GetItemImage(it.first).GetStock().isEmpty())
                 aImage = Image(StockImage::Yes, GetItemImage(it.first).GetStock());
             SetItemImage(it.first, aImage);
         }
     }
